Consequently
$$
\boxed{
\mathbb P(S_n=2k-n)
=\binom nkp^kq^{\,n-k},
\quad k=0,\ldots,n,
}
$$
and $S_n$ has probability zero at integers of the other parity. This is the finite-time law of a <simple random walk on the integer line>.

